hypotheses.statement:
There are a total function $g:\mathbb N\to\mathbb N$, a real constant $\delta>0$, and an integer $u_0\ge4$ such that the graph of $g$ has a single-fold Diophantine representation, including uniqueness of its output and every auxiliary coordinate for each input, and $$\label{eq:growth-bounds}
 \delta(\log u)^2<\log g(u)<u\log u
       \qquad(u\ge u_0).$$

For an integer $a\ge2$, put $D=a^2-1$ and define integers $x_i(a),y_i(a)$ by $$(a+\sqrt D)^i=x_i(a)+y_i(a)\sqrt D\qquad(i\ge0).$$ Every solution in positive integers of $x^2-Dy^2=1$ is $(x_i(a),y_i(a))$ for exactly one $i\ge1$. Moreover, $$\label{eq:pell-bounds}
 y_i(a)\equiv i\pmod{a-1},\qquad
 (2a-1)^{i-1}\le y_i(a)\le(2a)^{i-1}\quad(i\ge1).$$ If $b,u\ge2$ and $n\ge0$ are integers, then $$\label{eq:pell-ratio}
 b^n\le \frac{y_{n+1}(bu)}{y_{n+1}(u)}
 \le b^n\left(1+\frac1{2u-1}\right)^n.$$

