For each $L\ge2$, the size of $A_b$ is independent of $b$ and equals $$\label{eq:universe-size}
 N_L=\sum_{e\in E}3^{2|F(e)|+1}
       +\sum_{v\in V}3^{2f(v)+d(v)-1}.$$ In particular, $$L^3\le N_L\le (3^{10}+3^{29})L^3.$$ Every vertex has at least one configuration atom.

Let $\mathcal X$ be an $H$-invariant, membership-transitive finite family of hereditarily finite objects over $A_b$, and suppose $|\mathcal X|\le N^q$ for some fixed $q\ge0$. Every object in $\mathcal X$, including every recursive constituent of each of its members, has a $K$-support of length at most $2L(q\log_3N)^2$. All these supports can be padded to the common positive length $$\label{eq:support-length}
 s=\left\lceil2L(q\log_3N+1)^2\right\rceil+1
   =O_q\bigl(L(1+\log L)^2\bigr).$$

Let $T\subseteq E$ and $\sigma\in\mathbb F_3^T$. There is $k\in\ker\partial$ with $k|_T=\sigma$ if and only if, for every component $U$ of $G\setminus T$, $$\label{eq:component-balance}
 R_U:=\sum_{v\in U}\sum_{\substack{e\in T\\e\ni v}}
                      \epsilon_{ve}\sigma_e=0.$$ If an extension does not exist, there is a nonempty failing component with $$|U|\le L^3/2,\qquad |U|\le(|T|/c)^{3/2}.$$
